\s1 The Locusts, Fire, and Plumb Line
\r \ref Joel 2:1–11|JOL 2:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb showed me:|הִרְאַ֙נִי֙\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb He was preparing|יוֹצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb swarms of locusts|גֹּבַ֔י\rb* \rb just after|אַחַ֖ר\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb harvest,|גִּזֵּ֥י\rb* \rb as the late spring crop|עֲל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַלָּ֑קֶשׁ\rb* \rb was coming up.|בִּתְחִלַּ֖ת\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \ft LXX \fqa A swarm of locusts coming from the east; and, behold, one grasshopper, king Gog.\f* \rb |וְהִ֨נֵּה־\rb*\rb |לֶ֔קֶשׁ\rb*\v 2 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb when|אִם־\rb* \rb the locusts had|כִּלָּה֙\rb* \rb eaten|לֶֽאֱכוֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every green plant|עֵ֣שֶׂב\rb* \rb in the land,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb I said,|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb “Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִה֙\rb* \rb please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb forgive!|סְֽלַֽח־\rb* \rb How|מִ֥י\rb* \rb will Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb survive,|יָק֖וּם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is so small?”|קָטֹ֖ן\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb relented|נִחַ֥ם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb this plan.|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb “It will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb happen,”|תִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb He|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb said.|אָמַ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb showed me:|הִרְאַ֙נִי֙\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb The Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb was calling|קֹרֵ֛א\rb* \rb for judgment|לָרִ֥ב\rb* \rb by fire.|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb It consumed|וַתֹּ֙אכַל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the great|רַבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb deep|תְּה֣וֹם\rb* \rb and devoured|וְאָכְלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land.|הַחֵֽלֶק׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then I said,|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb* \rb “Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִה֙\rb* \rb please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb stop!|חֲדַל־\rb* \rb How|מִ֥י\rb* \rb will Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb survive,|יָק֖וּם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is so small?”|קָטֹ֖ן\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb relented|נִחַ֥ם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb this plan.|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb “It|הִיא֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb happen|תִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb either,”|גַּם־\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD.|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb He showed me:|הִרְאַ֔נִי\rb* \rb Behold,|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֛י\rb* \rb was standing|נִצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb a wall|חוֹמַ֣ת\rb* \rb true to plumb,|אֲנָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb with a plumb line|אֲנָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb in His hand.|וּבְיָד֖וֹ\rb* \v 8 \rb “Amos,|עָמ֔וֹס\rb* \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb see?”|רֹאֶה֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*
\p \rb “A plumb line,”|אֲנָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb I replied.|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*
\p \rb “Behold,”|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb* \rb “I am setting|שָׂ֤ם\rb* \rb a plumb line|אֲנָךְ֙\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel;|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb I will no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb spare|עֲב֥וֹר\rb* \rb them:|לֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb The high places|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Isaac|יִשְׂחָ֔ק\rb* \rb will be deserted,|וְנָשַׁ֙מּוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the sanctuaries|וּמִקְדְּשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will be laid waste;|יֶחֱרָ֑בוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb and I will rise up|וְקַמְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with My sword.”|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃פ\rb*
\s1 Amaziah Accuses Amos
\p \v 10 \rb Then Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָה֙\rb* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Amos|עָמ֗וֹס\rb* \rb has conspired|קָשַׁ֨ר\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb in the midst|בְּקֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb The land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb bear|לְהָכִ֖יל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his words,|דְּבָרָֽיו׃\rb* \v 11 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֙\rb* \rb Amos|עָמ֔וֹס\rb* \rb has said:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֣וּת\rb* \rb by the sword,|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb and Israel|וְיִ֨שְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will surely go into exile,|גָּלֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִגְלֶ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb away from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb their homeland.’”|אַדְמָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb And Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amos,|עָמ֔וֹס\rb* \rb “Go away,|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb you seer!|חֹזֶ֕ה\rb* \rb Flee|בְּרַח־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah;|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb earn your bread|וֶאֱכָל־\rb*\rb |לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb there|וְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and do your prophesying|תִּנָּבֵֽא׃\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \v 13 \rb But never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb prophesy|לְהִנָּבֵ֑א\rb*\rb |וּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb at Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb again,|תוֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb it is|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb the sanctuary|מִקְדַּשׁ־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and the temple|וּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the kingdom.”|מַמְלָכָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb “I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb was not|לֹא־\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Or \fqa I am not\f* \rb a prophet,”|נָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb Amos|עָמוֹס֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*\rb |אֲמַצְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb “nor was I the son|בֶן־\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Or \fqa nor am I the son\f* \rb of a prophet;|נָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb rather,|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb was a herdsman|בוֹקֵ֥ר\rb* \rb and|אָנֹ֖כִי\rb* \rb a tender|וּבוֹלֵ֥ס\rb* \rb of sycamore-fig trees.|שִׁקְמִֽים׃\rb* \v 15 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb took me|וַיִּקָּחֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb from following|מֵאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֑אן\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַי֙\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb ‘Go,|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel.’|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb hear|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say:|אֹמֵ֗ר\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb prophesy|תִנָּבֵא֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel;|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb preach|תַטִּ֖יף\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Isaac.’|יִשְׂחָֽק׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\q1 \rb ‘Your wife|אִשְׁתְּךָ֞\rb* \rb will become a prostitute|תִּזְנֶה֙\rb* \rb in the city,|בָּעִ֤יר\rb*
\q2 \rb and your sons|וּבָנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֔לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword.|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*
\q1 \rb Your land|וְאַדְמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb will be divided|תְּחֻלָּ֑ק\rb* \rb by a measuring line,|בַּחֶ֣בֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb and you yourself|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will die|תָּמ֔וּת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb pagan|טְמֵאָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 7:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa unclean\f* \rb soil.|אֲדָמָ֤ה\rb*
\q1 \rb And Israel|וְיִ֨שְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will surely go into exile,|גָּלֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִגְלֶ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb away from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb their homeland.’”|אַדְמָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*
\c 8
\s1 The Basket of Summer Fruit
\p \v 1 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb showed me:|הִרְאַ֖נִי\rb* \rb I saw|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb a basket|כְּל֥וּב\rb* \rb of summer fruit.|קָֽיִץ׃\rb*\f + \fr 8:1 \ft Or \fqa ripe fruit\ft ; also in verse 2\f*
\p \v 2 \rb “Amos,|עָמ֔וֹס\rb* \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb do you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb see?”|רֹאֶה֙\rb* \rb He asked.|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “A basket|כְּל֣וּב\rb* \rb of summer fruit,”|קָ֑יִץ\rb* \rb I replied.|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*
\p \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb “The end|הַקֵּץ֙\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel;|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb I will no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb spare|עֲב֥וֹר\rb* \rb them.”|לֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “In that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day,”|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb “the songs|שִׁיר֤וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 8:3 \ft Or \fqa the singing women\f* \rb of the temple|הֵיכָל֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:3 \ft Or \fqa palace\f* \rb will turn to wailing.|וְהֵילִ֜ילוּ\rb* \rb Many|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb will be the corpses,|הַפֶּ֔גֶר\rb* \rb strewn|הִשְׁלִ֥יךְ\rb* \rb in silence|הָֽס׃פ\rb* \rb everywhere!”|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |מָק֖וֹם\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Hear|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb this,|זֹ֕את\rb* \rb you who trample|הַשֹּׁאֲפִ֖ים\rb* \rb the needy,|אֶבְי֑וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb who do away with|וְלַשְׁבִּ֖ית\rb* \rb the poor|עַנְוֵי\rb* \rb of the land,|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb asking,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “When|מָתַ֞י\rb* \rb will the New Moon|הַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb be over,|יַעֲבֹ֤ר\rb*
\q2 \rb that we may sell|וְנַשְׁבִּ֣ירָה\rb* \rb grain?|שֶּׁ֔בֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb When will the Sabbath end,|וְהַשַּׁבָּ֖ת\rb*
\q2 \rb that we may market|וְנִפְתְּחָה־\rb* \rb wheat?|בָּ֑ר\rb*
\q1 \rb Let us reduce|לְהַקְטִ֤ין\rb* \rb the ephah|אֵיפָה֙\rb* \rb and increase|וּלְהַגְדִּ֣יל\rb* \rb the shekel;|שֶׁ֔קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 8:5 \ft Or \fqa Let us reduce the measure and increase the price\f*
\q2 \rb let us cheat|וּלְעַוֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb with dishonest|מִרְמָֽה׃\rb* \rb scales.|מֹאזְנֵ֥י\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb Let us buy|לִקְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb the poor|דַּלִּ֔ים\rb* \rb with silver|בַּכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the needy|וְאֶבְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb for|בַּעֲב֣וּר\rb* \rb a pair of sandals,|נַעֲלָ֑יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb selling|נַשְׁבִּֽיר׃\rb* \rb even the chaff|וּמַפַּ֥ל\rb* \rb with the wheat!”|בַּ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb by the Pride|בִּגְא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Jacob:|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*
\q1 \rb “I will never|אִם־\rb*\rb |לָנֶ֖צַח\rb* \rb forget|אֶשְׁכַּ֥ח\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of their deeds.|מַעֲשֵׂיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb quake|תִרְגַּ֣ז\rb* \rb for|הַ֤עַל\rb* \rb this,|זֹאת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its dwellers|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb mourn?|וְאָבַ֖ל\rb*
\q1 \rb All of it|כֻּלָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb will swell|וְעָלְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb like the Nile;|כָאֹר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb it will surge|וְנִגְרְשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb and then subside|וְנִשְׁקָה\rb*
\q2 \rb like the Nile|כִּיא֥וֹר\rb* \rb in Egypt.|מִצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb And in that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD,|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb I will make the sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb go down|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb* \rb at noon,|בַּֽצָּהֳרָ֑יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and I will darken|וְהַחֲשַׁכְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the earth|לָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb in the daytime.|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*\rb |אֽוֹר׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb I will turn|וְהָפַכְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb your feasts|חַגֵּיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb into mourning|לְאֵ֗בֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your songs|שִֽׁירֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb into lamentation.|לְקִינָ֔ה\rb*
\q1 \rb I will cause everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb to wear|וְהַעֲלֵיתִ֤י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |מָתְנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb sackcloth|שָׂ֔ק\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb*
